   "shape_h": "ol",
   "shape_m": "ol",
   "html_text": "Is weighing reasons for more than two alternatives just a free-for-all in which all reasons for all alternatives compete against each other all at once? Can something be a reason for φ relative to one alternative but not another? If something is a reason against φ, is it always a reason for each alternative? To weigh reasons properly, must all options be considered or are some options privileged or more important to consider than others?",
